From 5ac4d834fb68ed1b3d684af63bd59d43ae0c3483 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:52:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Receipts: cheques straight to bank; balances derived from
 receipts

Bank
- Cheques (like transfers) are credited to the bank chosen on the receipt
  when it is saved; edits/deletes add reversal lines. Bank Deposit now
  only carries cash plus cheques received before this change, so nothing
  is counted twice. Cheque/transfer-only collections are marked Banked.
- bank_transactions.channel (cheque/transfer/deposit/expense) + narration
  shown on the bank ledger; bank money columns widened to decimal(15,2).

Balances and advances
- Single-invoice create and edit go through the same ReceiptRecorder as
  the multi-invoice screen: invoice status/balance are derived from
  allocations, never chosen. Fixes edits subtracting twice, "completed"
  with money owed, fully paid invoices left open, negative balances on
  overpayment, WHT overwritten on edit, image wiped on edit, cashier
  replaced on edit.
- Overpayment refused unless kept as client credit; advance flag set
  automatically (credit kept, or paid before the invoice month).
- receipts.advance_payment boolean column made a string (it could never
  hold "advance" on MySQL).
- php artisan receipts:recompute [--apply --reopen-short
  --overpayments-to-credit --client=] repairs historic balances; dry run
  by default with a CSV report.

Tests: 43 passing on SQLite and MariaDB 10.11.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
